  "id": "3d_idol_image_to_gaussian_splat",
  "name": "IDOL — image to 3D",
  "title": "Turn a picture into 3D, with a turntable video",
  "summary": "Give it one picture of an object or a character and get a soft 3D \"splat\", a rough mesh and a short video that turns around it. A sibling of TripoSplat, with its own model.",
  "description": "IDOL, run through ComfyUI's TripoSplat nodes: one picture in, a 3D Gaussian splat out.\n\nUse a clean picture with the subject in the middle. Leave \"Remove the background\" on for a photo with a busy background; turn it off only for a PNG whose background is already transparent.\n\nOutputs: the splat (.spz) to spin in the splat viewer, a mesh (.glb) extracted from it, and a 3-second video orbiting the splat.",
  "category": "3d",
  "experimental": true,
  "tags": [
    "idol",
    "triposplat",
    "3d",
    "gaussian-splat",
    "image-to-3d"
